  (text "Charging (power board USB-C): plug a 5 V USB charger. The LED is on while charging.\nQ5 cuts VBAT (FC + motors) while USB is plugged in: no motor can spin during charging and\nthe charger terminates on the battery current alone. The FC can stay on its own USB for data.\nBattery: JST PH 2.0 pigtail on the pads J2 (rated 2 A), or a soldered lead (any current up to the shunt rating)."
    (at 60.96 228.6 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid "5408ff33-e41d-5af8-a3c3-f026d3814ea3"))
